Tia (docs): Heads-up — opening a docs PR to add slimline parser examples for tool-calling when the model returns nested arrays and optional fields. Need fast eyes on guardrail language, and parity across JS/Python SDK snippets. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1234
Sam (eng-runtime): Nice. Can you call out the runtime fallback we do when the JSON can't be parsed? It's important for the examples.
Tia (docs): Yep — I added a short note about automatic fallback to the compact envelope pattern. Thinking to show a malformed -> shim flow.
Jordan (devex): For SDK parity, we should show 1) streaming token-safe parse, 2) non-streaming retry with fallback. I can draft the JS streaming snippet.
Maria (sdk): Dropping a quick JS sample below. Will also port to Python after review.
Maria (sdk): ```js
// parse-with-fallback.js (SDK example)
const res = await redwood.responses.create({
  model: 'open-llm-7b',
  input: prompt,
});
try {
  const payload = JSON.parse(res.output[0].content);
  // prefer compact envelope: {"result": [...]} 
} catch (err) {
  // fallback: shim into {"result": [raw_text]} and call parseResult(payload)
}
```
Sam (eng-runtime): That matches what runtime does: if parse fails we emit `parse_shim_applied` telemetry and attempt envelope coercion. Can you add that telemetry note?
Tia (docs): Adding note and a one-liner about telemetry in the observability section.
Chad (product): Please include a short blurb about customer-visible behavior: downstream callers will see a 200 with `parsed=true|false` field in the route-level response. Keeps expectations clear.
Jordan (devex): Also let's include an example prompt that reproduces the nested-array edge case. Something like: "Return actions as an array of arrays: [[{name:..}]]" so folks can test locally.
Tia (docs): Good call. I'll add the sample prompt and a tiny test case in the PR description.
Maria (sdk): Python snippet coming up — will mirror the try/except shim and show `client.responses.parse_shim`.
Tia (docs): One more ask: can someone grep for old links to `/tool-calling` and `/structured-output` and add redirects? I found a couple broken anchors.
Jordan (devex): On it. I'll run a link-checker in CI and push a tiny action to flag those anchors.
deploy-bot: Deployment preview for PR #1234 is ready: https://deploy-preview.redwood-inference.dev/docs/1234 (checks: lint ✅, link-checker ⚠️ (anchors))
Sam (eng-runtime): Ping me when CI shows the anchor warnings. I'll adjust the runtime docs if we need to change wording to match new anchors.
Tia (docs): Thanks everyone — plan: update PR with the JS/Python snippets, add the prompt/test, include telemetry and product notes, and resolve anchor fixes. Target: ship EOD tomorrow. :shipit: 
Maria (sdk): Quick nit: in the JS example, prefer `res.output_text` rather than indexing output[0] — more realistic for streaming and multi-output routes. I'll send a tiny patch.
Tia (docs): Perfect. If no objections I’ll merge after fixes and a saner README addition with migration guidance.
Chad (product): No objections. Appreciate the concise migration note for customers on Dedicated.
Jordan (devex): I left one inline comment on the PR around the fallback snippet clarity.
Tia (docs): Acknowledged. Closing loop here — will ping thread when updated.
